      "closure_rationale": "Reader/writer exclusion is defined by exact touched-element set intersection and at least one writer, independently of pointer lifetime. Interleaved even/odd writer sets refute necessity of disjoint bounding intervals. Raw aliases, copied controls and fabricated extents remain caller violations; a live token does not validate arbitrary native storage. Explicit C release is compared with the existing inspected RefCell guarded lifetime contract without claiming equivalent enforcement. Actual ow_borrow/ow_release/ow_split are composed unchanged with a separate64-element exact strided book. Overflow-safe extent subtraction bounds row/column products, duplicate touched indices reject, and empty sets require no derived address. Acquire/release use fixed book identity and finite serial retirement. Split stages both children, accounts for retired parent capacity and rebinds candidate token pointers before publication. Six C17 profiles execute seven anchors, eight compiled semantic controls and seven compiling-stub rejections. Independent integer products/sets check35084interval pairs,31200shapes,9216read-write intersections over46distinct small sets and576split/capacity/serial cases. Logical field comparisons and output canaries check failed whole-book transactions. Actual OW_MUTANT4/14 retain ordinary interval regressions; SIZE_MAX is numeric validation only. The required changed variant is implemented with both row and column partitioning over actual padded int32_t arrays. Tests prove the selected child indices8,9,14,15 change while padding and unrelated cells remain unchanged. Empty right children keep a valid offset instead of inventing an out-of-extent next-row address. Exact disjoint union, old-token invalidation, final retirement and explicit bounded O(N squared) costs are assessed separately. Independent delayed learner performance remains unassessed. Bounded author support only."
    },
